    fix(graph): bound the full graph understand response by --budget (DF-WARPFS-158)
    
    The harmonic formatter now charges MAP, SIGNATURES, DETAIL and the thin-task
    footer against one token_budget*4 char budget instead of leaking MAP and
    SIGNATURES unbounded and breaking DETAIL on the first oversized block:
    
    - per-tier allocations (15/25/60) with skip-not-break block fitting, so one
      oversized detail block can no longer empty the DETAIL tier;
    - when no detail block fits, the empty-tier message names the skipped file
      and its block size;
    - a defensive whole-response truncation keeps the rendered answer inside the
      stated budget (with a 256-char structural floor for tiny budgets);
    - new tests: understand_harmonic_output_stays_within_total_budget and
      understand_budget_1000_is_strictly_smaller_than_6000.
    
    Live acceptance (task-router@d643ef4, 314-file warmed corpus): default budget
    19,613 chars (<= 24,000) with real DETAIL blocks; --budget 1000 -> 725 chars
    vs --budget 6000 -> 19,613; empty DETAIL names the skipped file and size.
    Guard scripts/rust-lint.sh green (clippy -D warnings clean, 563/563).
    
